# MC (MEMORY CHANNEL) — Set-direction wire frames, hand-derived
#
# Manual: "FT-991A HF/VHF/UHF ALL MODE TRANSCEIVER — CAT Operation Reference Manual",
#   YAESU MUSEN CO., LTD., Copyright 2017.
# Printed revision: "1711-D" (back cover, PDF page 20). No revision on the title page.
# Chart used: the MC command detail block, printed folio 11 = PDF page 12.
#   Layout counted from the SET chart (the brief asks for Set frames). The ANSWER chart in
#   the same block was counted independently and is the identical 6-position layout; the
#   READ chart is a 3-position layout ("M C ;"). All three are recorded below.
# Derivation date: 05/09/2026.
# NO code, no generator, no other file and no other document was consulted.
#
# COUNTED FRAME LENGTH (Set): 6 bytes, terminator included.
#   Count A (left-to-right): 1 "M", 2 "C", 3 P1, 4 P1, 5 P1, 6 ";", 7..10 empty.
#   Count B (row totals): 1 printed row x 10 numbered cells; filled cells = 6. Agree; no
#   third look needed. Chart and legend cropped and re-rendered at 600 dpi.
#   Read chart: 3 bytes ("M C ;", cells 1..3 filled, 4..10 empty).
#   Answer chart: 6 bytes ("M C P1 P1 P1 ;", cells 1..6 filled).
#
# POSITION-BY-POSITION FIELD MAP (Set chart, MC block, printed folio 11)
#   pos 1      "M"                     printed literally
#   pos 2      "C"                     printed literally
#   pos 3-5    P1  (3 positions)       MC legend, verbatim and complete:
#                                        "P1   001 - 117: Memory Channel Number"
#                                        "     001 - 099: Regular Memory Channel"
#                                        "     100: P-1L    101: P-1U ~ 116: P-9L    117: P-9U"
#   pos 6      ";"                     terminator, printed literally
#
# DO THE MC AND THE MR/MT/MW SLOT LEGENDS LIST THE SAME RANGES? — BOTH recorded verbatim,
# not resolved.
#   MC legend (printed folio 11, PDF page 12), verbatim:
#     "P1   001 - 117: Memory Channel Number"
#     "     001 - 099: Regular Memory Channel"
#     "     100: P-1L    101: P-1U ~ 116: P-9L    117: P-9U"
#   MR legend (printed folio 12, PDF page 13), verbatim:  "P0/1  001-117 (Memory Channel)"
#   MT legend (printed folio 12, PDF page 13), verbatim:  "P0/1  001-117 (Memory Channel)"
#   MW legend (printed folio 12, PDF page 13), verbatim:  "P1  001-117 (Memory Channel)"
#   They do NOT list the same ranges: MC is the only legend in this manual that breaks the
#   span down into a regular range and a PMS range and that spells any PMS slot. MR, MT and
#   MW print the outer span 001-117 and nothing else. The outer spans themselves match.
#   Recorded, not resolved.
#
# ID COMMAND ANSWER FRAME, exactly as printed (ID block, printed folio 10 = PDF page 11)
#   Answer chart positions: 1 "I", 2 "D", 3 P1, 4 P1, 5 P1, 6 P1, 7 ";" — counted 7 bytes.
#   Legend, verbatim: "P1   0670: FT-991A"
#   Answer frame:                                    ID0670;
#   (For completeness: the ID Read request chart prints "I D ;" — 3 bytes: ID;
#    and the ID Set chart is printed as an empty grid.)
#
# MODE LEGEND ON THE MEMORY COMMANDS vs ON THE MD COMMAND — BOTH verbatim, not resolved
#   On the memory commands MR, MT and MW (printed folio 12, PDF page 13), P6 reads:
#     "P6  MODE  1: LSB   2: USB   3: CW   4: FM   5: AM   6: RTTY-LSB   7: CW-R"
#     "          8: DATA-LSB   9: RTTY-USB   A: DATA-FM   B: FM-N   C: DATA-USB"
#     "          D: AM-N   E: C4FM"
#   On the MD (OPERATING MODE) command (printed folio 11, PDF page 12), P2 reads:
#     "P2   MODE        1: LSB    2: USB    3: CW-U    4: FM    5: AM    6: RTTY-LSB"
#     "                 7: CW-L    8: DATA-LSB    9: RTTY-USB    A: DATA-FM"
#     "                 B: FM-N    C: DATA-USB    D: AM-N    E: C4FM"
#   They differ at two indices: index 3 is "CW" on the memory commands and "CW-U" on MD;
#   index 7 is "CW-R" on the memory commands and "CW-L" on MD. Every other index and label
#   is identical. Recorded, not resolved.
#   (A third mode legend, identical to the memory-command wording, is printed on the IF
#   command, printed folio 10 = PDF page 11.)
#
# BYTES THE MANUAL DETERMINES vs INHERITED-ASSUMED
#   Manual-determined: "MC"; the 3-digit P1 width (counted); ";"; the P1 range 001-117 and
#   the PMS slot numbers and spellings quoted above.
#   INHERITED-ASSUMED: none. Every byte of every MC vector below is fixed by the chart and
#   the legend.
#
# Hardware status: UNVERIFIED. No frame below has been sent to or read from a radio.
#
mc_ch012_regular_memory_channel	MC012;
mc_ch099_last_regular_memory_channel	MC099;
mc_ch100_first_pms_slot_p_1l	MC100;
mc_ch117_last_pms_slot_p_9u	MC117;
